# The owner's phone driver runs on Windows Git Bash, and the repo has no server
# between us and the user's machine. Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true
# by default, which converts text files to CRLF on checkout there; a CRLF bash script
# fails with stray-\r errors and a CRLF python helper is not the file CI tested.
# Shell and python are therefore LF-pinned everywhere so a fresh clone behaves like
# the file-by-file downloads the driver was first written for.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf

# Binary by nature; never touch. (The store assets and evidence screenshots live here,
# and any release artifacts copied in by the owner on the device-run machine.)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
